# 必考词 Unit06
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2023红宝书考研英语词汇-必考词
# 描述: 必考词Unit06核心高频词汇

{{coordinate}}{/kəʊˈɔːrdɪneɪt/}{{v. 协调；配合}}{{The manager coordinated the efforts of different teams.}}

{{cope}}{/kəʊp/}}{v. 应对；处理}}{{She learned to cope with stress through meditation.}}

{{core}}{/kɔːr/}}{n. 核心；要点}}{{Innovation is the core of the company's strategy.}}

{{corporate}}{/ˈkɔːrpərət/}}{adj. 公司的；法人的}}{{The corporate culture emphasizes teamwork and innovation.}}

{{correspond}}{/ˌkɒrɪˈspɒnd/}}{v. 通信；对应}}{{The results correspond with our expectations.}}

{{corrupt}}{/kəˈrʌpt/}}{adj. 腐败的；v. 使腐化}}{{The corrupt officials were arrested and prosecuted.}}

{{counsel}}{/ˈkaʊnsl/}}{n. 忠告；律师；v. 建议}}{{The lawyer provided counsel to his client before the trial.}}

{{counterpart}}{/ˈkaʊntərpɑːrt/}}{n. 对应的人或物}}{{The CEO met with her counterpart from the rival company.}}

{{couple}}{/ˈkʌpl/}}{n. 一对；几个；v. 连接}}{{A couple of students volunteered for the project.}}

{{crash}}{/kræʃ/}}{v./n. 碰撞；崩溃}}{{The stock market crash affected millions of investors.}}

{{create}}{/kriˈeɪt/}}{v. 创造；创建}}{{The artist created a masterpiece in just three months.}}

{{credit}}{/ˈkredɪt/}}{n. 信用；学分；功劳}}{{She deserves credit for the success of the project.}}

{{criminal}}{/ˈkrɪmɪnl/}}{adj. 犯罪的；n. 罪犯}}{{The criminal was sentenced to ten years in prison.}}

{{crisis}}{/ˈkraɪsɪs/}}{n. 危机；紧要关头}}{{The financial crisis of 2008 had global consequences.}}

{{criteria}}{/kraɪˈtɪəriə/}}{n. 标准；准则（复数）}}{{The selection criteria include academic performance and experience.}}

{{critical}}{/ˈkrɪtɪkl/}}{adj. 批评的；关键的；危急的}}{{Critical thinking is an essential skill for students.}}

{{crucial}}{/ˈkruːʃl/}}{adj. 至关重要的；决定性的}}{{Education plays a crucial role in personal development.}}

{{cultivate}}{/ˈkʌltɪveɪt/}}{v. 培养；耕种}}{{Schools should cultivate students' creativity and independence.}}

{{cure}}{/kjʊər/}}{n. 治愈；治疗方法；v. 治愈}}{{Scientists are working to find a cure for the disease.}}

{{curiosity}}{/ˌkjʊəriˈɒsəti/}}{n. 好奇心；好奇}}{{Children have a natural curiosity about the world.}}

{{current}}{/ˈkʌrənt/}}{adj. 当前的；n. 水流；电流}}{{The current situation requires immediate action.}}

{{curriculum}}{/kəˈrɪkjələm/}}{n. 课程；课程表}}{{The school revised its curriculum to include more practical courses.}}

{{custom}}{/ˈkʌstəm/}}{n. 习惯；风俗；海关}}{{It is a local custom to celebrate the harvest festival.}}

{{cycle}}{/ˈsaɪkl/}}{n. 循环；周期}}{{The business cycle affects employment and investment.}}

{{deadline}}{/ˈdedlaɪn/}}{n. 截止日期}}{{The deadline for submitting the report is next Friday.}}

{{debate}}{/dɪˈbeɪt/}}{n./v. 辩论；争论}}{{The debate over immigration policy continues to divide the nation.}}

{{decade}}{/ˈdekeɪd/}}{n. 十年}}{{Technology has advanced dramatically over the past decade.}}

{{decline}}{/dɪˈklaɪn/}}{v./n. 下降；拒绝}}{{The population of the species has declined sharply in recent years.}}

{{dedicate}}{/ˈdedɪkeɪt/}}{v. 奉献；致力于}}{{She dedicated her life to helping the poor.}}

{{defeat}}{/dɪˈfiːt/}}{v./n. 击败；失败}}{{The team suffered a bitter defeat in the final match.}}

{{defend}}{/dɪˈfend/}}{v. 防御；辩护}}{{The lawyer defended his client against the charges.}}

{{define}}{/dɪˈfaɪn/}}{v. 定义；限定}}{{It is difficult to define the concept of happiness.}}

{{delay}}{/dɪˈleɪ/}}{v./n. 耽搁；延迟}}{{The flight was delayed due to bad weather.}}

{{deliberate}}{/dɪˈlɪbərət/}}{adj. 故意的；慎重的}}{{It was a deliberate attempt to mislead the public.}}

{{delicate}}{/ˈdelɪkət/}}{adj. 精致的；微妙的}}{{The negotiations require a delicate approach.}}

{{deliver}}{/dɪˈlɪvər/}}{v. 递送；发表；接生}}{{The courier delivered the package to the office.}}

{{demand}}{/dɪˈmɑːnd/}}{v./n. 要求；需求}}{{There is a growing demand for renewable energy sources.}}

{{democracy}}{/dɪˈmɒkrəsi/}}{n. 民主；民主制度}}{{Democracy allows citizens to participate in government decisions.}}

{{demonstrate}}{/ˈdemənstreɪt/}}{v. 证明；演示；示威}}{{The experiment demonstrates the principles of physics.}}

{{deny}}{/dɪˈnaɪ/}}{v. 否认；拒绝}}{{He denied any involvement in the scandal.}}
